  "description": "Dry-run-only matter must not count as correspondence.",
  "why_it_exists": "Inbound replies used to be attached to a matter by scanning for a [MAT-...] tag anywhere in the message, including quoted history, and with no check that the sender was anyone this matter had ever written to. That let an unrelated or hostile message attach itself to a live legal matter and append actions to it. The policy became thread-first, fail-closed, with the sender required to be a recorded party.",
