  "expect": {
    "decision": "BLOCKED",
    "basis": "NO_CORRESPONDENCE",
    "matter_id": "MAT-20260101-012",
    "write_log_inbound": false,
    "write_append_action": false,
    "write_touch_matter": false
  },
  "assertions": [
    "resolveReply(event, register).decision is BLOCKED",
    "basis is NO_CORRESPONDENCE",
    "matter_id is MAT-20260101-012",
    "write_log_inbound, write_append_action and write_touch_matter are all false: nothing is mutated",
    "OUTBOUND_DRY_RUN is not in REAL_OUTBOUND, so a matter that has only ever dry-run has no parties",
    "a reply to a message that was never actually sent cannot be accepted",
    "MERGED from wf5-reply-dry-run-is-not-correspondence (QA - WF5 Reply Matching Verification, VelAeCU71KHELUJP): the adapter field unverified_kind carries the basis, so an unverified reply on a dry-run-only matter reports NO_CORRESPONDENCE and not SENDER_NOT_A_PARTY.",
    "MERGED: sender_verified is false and matched is false; an unverified reply writes an Events row and nothing else - no action, no classification, no matter update.",
    "MERGED (KNOWN GAP, not asserted here): the deployed Build Reply Context seeds known parties from resolveReply's REAL_OUTBOUND rows only, but the wider WF5 reply path also reads Actions.recipient, which readmits a never-sent recipient. The proposed replacement derives known parties from real OUTBOUND correspondence only and was not deployed."
